  "read": "The morning expected a tech-led risk-on day with no U.S. red event, driven by earnings and Iran headlines, and that tone held, though not in a straight line. SPY opened about 0.26% higher, slipped below its opening range and filled the gap at 10:20 AM (low 765.21), then turned and climbed most of the day to a 771.14 high at 3:45 PM, closing at 769.52 (+0.54%, +0.28% from the open) while QQQ led at 720.65 (+1.19%). There was no U.S. scheduled event to grade; earnings and the AI trade did the work, with chip and AI names (AMD, AVGO, CDNS) lifting QQQ while Boeing fell almost 11% and the equal-weight RSP lagged through 10:30. The VIX eased to 17.52 (-4.7%), WTI fell 1.6% to about $100.11, and the 10-year yield ended flat near 4.99%. One plain observation: the 10:20 dip to fill the gap was the day's turn, and it came while QQQ held above its open, so the tech lead showed up early even when SPY looked soft; note also that the Fed decision is tomorrow, not later in the week as this morning's read put it. Tomorrow's first red event is the UK Annual Budget Release at 8:30 AM ET; the first U.S. one is the Fed rate decision at 2:00 PM ET, with the press conference at 2:30 PM.",
